Article 6

Every Woman has the right to:

a. live and maintain life as well as improve their standard of living;
b. meet their basic needs to grow and develop properly, form a family and continue their lineage;
c. develop their personality, obtain education, and improve their quality of life to become a person who is faithful, pious, responsible, of noble character, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or being enslaved and threats; g. obtain protection of self, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
h. obtain welfare and a decent life; i. participate in politics;
j. perform legal acts; and
k. freely choose a partner in marriage in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

