b. organizing;

c. implementation;

d. coordination;

e. budgeting;

f. supervision;

g. research and development;

h. standardization; and

i. management of development information in the Region. (3) The authority and responsibility for the Empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations. (4) The implementation of the authority and responsibility of the Regional Government shall be carried out through coordination with other Regional Apparatus that have authority over fields in the Empowerment of Women and Protection of Women.

